{"id": "permit-maze-permits-to-finish-permits", "title": "The permit maze: permits to finish permits, plans that wait, and a paid way through", "seconds": 138.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "e776ccea99898f45", "words": 405, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "In San Francisco, some building permits build nothing. Their only job is to finish an earlier permit.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.07, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A permit to finish a permit", "sub": "nothing new is built"}, "emph": ["nothing"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.28, 0.93, 1.13, 1.47, 1.87, 2.14, 2.7, 2.93, 3.21, 3.46, 3.57, 3.66, 3.97, 4.06, 4.46]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "Since 2015, how many of those has the City issued?", "t0": 5.19, "t1": 8.5, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Since 2015", "sub": "permits taken out only to finish, renew or reinstate"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.45, 1.22, 1.32, 1.56, 1.63, 1.83, 1.97, 2.12, 2.38]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "8,860.", "t0": 8.5, "t1": 10.8, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "8,860", "label": "permits only to finish an earlier permit", "sub": "2.6% of all filed"}, "emph": ["8,860"], "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.81, 1.13, 1.52]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.32, "t1": 12.77, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.15, 0.26, 0.81, 0.95, 1.03]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[8]", "established[12]"], "text": "How? A permit lasts 365 days.", "t0": 12.89, "t1": 15.8, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Permit issued", "sub": "lasts 365 days"}, {"art": "calendar", "name": "The job waits", "sub": "the permit lapses"}, {"art": "money", "name": "A new permit", "sub": "a new fee, the same queue"}], "kicker": "How the loop works"}, "emph": ["365 days"], "wt": [0.0, 0.54, 0.82, 1.15, 1.41, 1.61, 1.91, 2.45]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[8]"], "text": "If it lapses before the final inspection, the fix is a new permit, priced on the unfinished work.", "t0": 15.92, "t1": 20.46, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Permit issued", "sub": "lasts 365 days"}, {"art": "calendar", "name": "The job waits", "sub": "the permit lapses"}, {"art": "money", "name": "A new permit", "sub": "a new fee, the same queue"}], "kicker": "How the loop works"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.19, 0.57, 0.82, 0.91, 1.18, 1.82, 1.93, 2.18, 2.3, 2.38, 2.59, 3.24, 3.51, 3.62, 3.71, 4.2]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "Now take one home remodel. How many permits did it carry?", "t0": 20.68, "t1": 23.46, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "A home remodel", "kicker": "One job", "sub": "$100,000 to $1 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.36, 0.5, 0.71, 1.22, 1.55, 1.7, 2.02, 2.15, 2.25]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "A median of 7.", "t0": 23.46, "t1": 25.14, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "7", "label": "permits, the median remodel", "sub": "records from 4 departments, 565 days to sign-off"}, "emph": ["A"], "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.58, 0.74]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "A new building with five or more homes? 45 permits, each with its own fee and expiry date.", "t0": 25.66, "t1": 31.54, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["home remodel", "7 permits"], "b": ["new building, five or more homes", "45 permits"], "mid": "6.2 years"}, "emph": ["45 permits"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.24, 0.63, 0.77, 0.98, 1.11, 1.33, 1.96, 3.06, 3.79, 4.03, 4.17, 4.32, 4.55, 4.83, 5.01, 5.53]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "Then the plans wait. In full review, how many were put on hold at least once?", "t0": 31.76, "t1": 35.81, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Full plan review", "kicker": "Plans that wait", "sub": "5 review stations in 4 departments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.21, 0.55, 0.98, 1.35, 1.62, 2.19, 2.32, 2.45, 2.59, 2.74, 2.87, 3.07, 3.19, 3.44]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "share", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "65 percent.", "t0": 35.81, "t1": 37.73, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 65, "label": "of full-review plans put on hold at least once"}, "emph": ["65 percent"], "wt": [0.04, 1.37]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[9]"], "text": "The City’s own clock: of 127,033 finished first reviews,", "t0": 38.25, "t1": 44.01, "shot": "b9c0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "127,033", "label": "finished first reviews", "sub": "The City’s own clock"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.34, 0.57, 1.25, 1.74, 1.92, 2.21, 2.8, 3.22, 3.89, 4.48, 4.82]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "share", "ref": ["established[9]"], "text": "77 percent missed its 30-day deadline.", "t0": 44.01, "t1": 46.73, "shot": "b9c", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 77, "label": "of 127,033 finished first reviews missed the City’s 30-day deadline", "kicker": "The City’s own clock"}, "emph": ["77 percent"], "wt": [0.04, 0.72, 1.18, 1.5, 1.64, 2.12]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[10]"], "text": "On time: 11 percent of 2021 permits, 73 percent of 2025’s,", "t0": 47.15, "t1": 52.67, "shot": "b9d", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["filed in 2021, on time", "11%"], "b": ["filed in 2025, on time", "73%"], "kicker": "Recent years count only finished reviews"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.68, 1.19, 1.62, 1.7, 1.97, 2.4, 3.23, 3.72, 4.13, 4.29, 4.44]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[10]"], "text": "though recent years count only finished reviews.", "t0": 52.67, "t1": 54.76, "shot": "b9dx", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Recent years", "sub": "count only finished reviews"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.19, 0.46, 0.73, 0.99, 1.19, 1.55]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[11]"], "text": "And Building plan check saw 57 percent of full-review permits more than once.", "t0": 54.88, "t1": 58.69, "shot": "b9e", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Building plan check", "kicker": "Seen more than once", "sub": "2.38 visits per permit", "chip": "57%"}, "emph": ["57 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.66, 0.98, 1.18, 1.72, 2.09, 2.17, 2.65, 3.04, 3.23, 3.4]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "Many owners hire a guide, a permit consultant.", "t0": 58.91, "t1": 61.38, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Permit consultants", "kicker": "A paid way through", "sub": "12,196 permits, 2015 to 2024", "chip": "$6.7 million"}, "wt": [0.11, 0.19, 0.51, 0.7, 0.8, 1.37, 1.44, 1.73]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "46 consultants and firms reported 6.7 million dollars in client fees.", "t0": 61.5, "t1": 66.08, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Permit consultants", "kicker": "A paid way through", "sub": "12,196 permits, 2015 to 2024", "chip": "$6.7 million"}, "emph": ["6.7 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.48, 0.92, 1.05, 1.51, 2.16, 2.35, 2.61, 2.81, 3.16, 3.53, 3.62, 4.0]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[13]"], "text": "They must report only on major projects, over 1,000,000 dollars.", "t0": 66.2, "t1": 69.57, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Permit consultants", "kicker": "A paid way through", "sub": "12,196 permits, 2015 to 2024", "chip": "$6.7 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.28, 0.62, 0.88, 1.01, 1.29, 1.86, 2.26, 2.41, 2.76]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "Does that buy speed? In full plan review, yes. 229 days against 289.", "t0": 69.69, "t1": 75.39, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["full review, with a consultant", "229 days"], "b": ["like permits without one", "289 days"]}, "emph": ["229"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.26, 0.43, 0.98, 1.32, 1.48, 1.73, 2.24, 2.71, 3.19, 3.47, 3.97, 4.33, 4.66, 4.79, 5.06]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "share", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "story[4]"], "text": "But across all permits, the consultant was faster only 44 percent of the time.", "t0": 75.51, "t1": 79.66, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 44, "label": "of permits where the consultant was faster"}, "emph": ["44 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.02, 0.38, 0.64, 1.39, 1.48, 1.89, 2.09, 2.43, 2.7, 3.22, 3.53, 3.59, 3.71]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[12]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Is speed bought? Firms with donations, lobbying or other links were no faster as a group.", "t0": 79.78, "t1": 84.12, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["firms with donations, lobbying or other links", "48%"], "b": ["like firms with none", "47%"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["no faster"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.81, 1.1, 1.26, 1.86, 2.32, 2.46, 2.72, 2.98, 3.17, 3.28, 3.7, 3.78, 3.87]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Before the City even takes the plans, there are 57 published requirements.", "t0": 84.34, "t1": 88.32, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Bought before the City takes the plans", "kicker": "57 published requirements", "sub": "architects, engineers, insurance, bonds", "chip": "36 pay a private party"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.29, 0.54, 0.76, 1.05, 1.17, 1.86, 2.0, 2.16, 2.81, 3.29]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "36 send money to private professionals or insurers, at prices the City doesn’t set.", "t0": 88.44, "t1": 93.45, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Bought before the City takes the plans", "kicker": "57 published requirements", "sub": "architects, engineers, insurance, bonds", "chip": "36 pay a private party"}, "emph": ["36"], "wt": [0.0, 0.6, 0.91, 1.18, 1.3, 1.58, 2.27, 2.46, 3.29, 3.41, 3.88, 4.0, 4.3, 4.62]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "Then the City’s own fees.", "t0": 93.57, "t1": 94.81, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fiscal 2019, a permit", "$1,126"], "b": ["fiscal 2026, a permit", "$1,781"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.16, 0.49, 0.73]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "Building Inspection took in 1,126 dollars a permit in 2019.", "t0": 94.93, "t1": 99.63, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fiscal 2019, a permit", "$1,126"], "b": ["fiscal 2026, a permit", "$1,781"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.68, 0.96, 1.12, 1.28, 1.76, 1.99, 2.28, 2.93, 3.29, 3.4, 3.76, 3.92, 4.15]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "In 2026, 1,781.", "t0": 99.75, "t1": 102.55, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fiscal 2019, a permit", "$1,126"], "b": ["fiscal 2026, a permit", "$1,781"]}, "emph": ["1,781"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.36, 1.08, 1.17, 1.52, 1.83, 2.11]}, {"scene": "official", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[2]", "established[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "Official reviewers have flagged this maze. In 2021, improper expedited permitting.", "t0": 102.77, "t1": 108.02, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "magnifier", "name": "Controller and City Attorney", "sub": "2021"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "City Attorney", "sub": "2022"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Civil Grand Jury", "sub": "2023"}], "kicker": "Official findings"}, "emph": ["2021"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.81, 0.96, 1.28, 1.46, 2.14, 2.61, 2.82, 3.83, 4.24, 4.76]}, {"scene": "official", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[2]", "established[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "In 2023, no check on promised 30-day permits.", "t0": 108.14, "t1": 111.41, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "magnifier", "name": "Controller and City Attorney", "sub": "2021"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "City Attorney", "sub": "2022"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Civil Grand Jury", "sub": "2023"}], "kicker": "Official findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.3, 1.24, 1.4, 1.78, 1.91, 2.3, 2.66]}, {"scene": "official", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[1]", "established[5]"], "text": "In 2026, the Board’s analyst found 280 days for a housing permit, the longest compared.", "t0": 111.53, "t1": 117.25, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "State housing department", "sub": "523 days to entitle"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Board’s analyst, 2024", "sub": "$1.6 million in fees waived"}, {"art": "calendar", "name": "Board’s analyst, 2026", "sub": "280 days, the longest compared"}], "kicker": "Official findings"}, "emph": ["280 days"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.29, 1.2, 1.29, 1.63, 2.04, 2.37, 2.55, 2.83, 3.18, 3.48, 3.62, 3.68, 3.96, 4.62, 4.76, 5.11]}, {"scene": "official", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "15 State letters are on file. 4 record an adverse finding, like a notice of violation.", "t0": 117.37, "t1": 122.49, "shot": "b20s", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "4", "label": "of 15 State letters on file record an adverse finding", "sub": "2021 to 2023; the last findings closed 16 January 2024"}, "emph": ["4"], "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.68, 0.93, 1.02, 1.18, 1.75, 2.49, 2.8, 2.9, 3.31, 3.87, 4.01, 4.09, 4.34, 4.44]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The records don’t show a true catch-22, or what stalled any one permit.", "t0": 122.71, "t1": 126.66, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["A true catch-22", "Why a given permit stalled"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.38, 0.58, 0.81, 0.92, 1.13, 2.37, 2.45, 2.65, 2.99, 3.21, 3.47]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? Each department’s rules for skipping the line, and who paid for faster review.", "t0": 126.78, "t1": 131.6, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Each department’s written guidelines for exceptions to the order of receipt"}, {"who": "", "what": "Who bought premium plan review, permit by permit"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.31, 0.6, 0.93, 1.5, 1.98, 2.23, 2.36, 2.63, 2.8, 3.3, 3.43, 3.59, 3.83, 3.99, 4.39]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "This file alleges nothing against any applicant, consultant or employee.", "t0": 131.72, "t1": 135.08, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.4, 0.72, 1.0, 1.35, 1.6, 2.19, 2.62, 2.81]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 135.2, "t1": 137.65, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.49, 0.57, 1.38, 1.63, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "One job, many permits", "lead2": "Plans that wait", "lead3": "A paid way through?", "lead4": "Fewer permits, more money", "official": "What reviewers found", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "flow", "hook": "question"}